{:edb/db-before-t 485 :edb/db-after-t 486 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533798 50 #inst "2026-10-05T00:50:43.865Z" 13194139533798 true] [17592186083065 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251825 13194139533798 true] [17592186083065 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251832 13194139533798 true] [17592186083065 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251839 13194139533798 true] [17592186083065 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251888 13194139533798 true] [17592186083066 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251874 13194139533798 true] [17592186083066 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251895 13194139533798 true] [17592186083066 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251916 13194139533798 true] [17592186083066 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251937 13194139533798 true] [17592186083067 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251881 13194139533798 true] [17592186083067 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251902 13194139533798 true] [17592186083067 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251909 13194139533798 true] [17592186083067 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251923 13194139533798 true] [17592186083067 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251930 13194139533798 true] [17592186083068 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251846 13194139533798 true] [17592186083068 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251853 13194139533798 true] [17592186083068 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251860 13194139533798 true] [17592186083068 1020 #edb/ref 17592186251867 13194139533798 true] [17592186083786 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533798 true] [17592186083786 1145 "The vertical asymptotes of the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ coincide with the zeros of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the vertical asymptotes of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(4x+1)-2,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(4x+1).$ This gives\n\n$$\n4x+1=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+1 & =n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & =-1+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4},$ where $n$ is an integer." 13194139533798 true] [17592186083787 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533798 true] [17592186083787 1145 "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{sec}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=3.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$" 13194139533798 true] [17592186083790 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533798 true] [17592186083790 1145 "On a negative branch of the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\le -1.\n$$\n\nThe points where $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-1$ are local maximums of the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$ \n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\le -1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $\\frac{1}{2}$ and adding $2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\le -1 \\\\  & \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\le -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})+2\\le -\\frac{1}{2}+2 \\\\  & f(x)\\le \\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\frac{3}{2}$ at the local maximum points." 13194139533798 true] [17592186251825 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251826 13194139533798 true] [17592186251825 1089 "q-117749" 13194139533798 true] [17592186251825 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533798 true] [17592186251825 1100 "Calculate the period of the function $y=2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$" 13194139533798 true] [17592186251825 1113 #uuid "5c406461-cb37-5308-b065-fa43ddd0d204" 13194139533798 true] [17592186251825 1145 "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{csc}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=6.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" 13194139533798 true] [17592186251826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251827 13194139533798 true] [17592186251826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251828 13194139533798 true] [17592186251826 1000